    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ccbbf0f_16e8ea2c",
        "filename": "compiler/optimizing/code_generator_riscv64.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5496,
      "author": {
        "id": 1018108
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T17:35:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For `int` left operand, we need to use only 5 bits from the right operand but these riscv64 instructions use 6 bits. And there is no `Bsetw`/`Bextw`/`Bclrw`/`Binvw` that would work on 32-bit values and take only 5 bits from the right operand.\n\nWe can get a scratch register and insert an explicit `ANDI scratch, rs2, 0x1f` but then the value of the optimization is questionable for three of these when we just replace two instructions with another two instructions. (The `Bclr` case is different as it replaces 3 instructions.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5496,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 5496,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "95bb2e208e9a90d1ac447de64bac99bc7ccb7e47",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a6a07d3c_0765aae7",
        "filename": "compiler/optimizing/code_generator_riscv64.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5496,
      "author": {
        "id": 3575424
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-24T19:37:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I’d prefer to fix `int` case and keep the transformation for `int` to avoid overcomplicating the code in `instruction_simplifier_riscv64.cc` excluding cases `bext/bset/binv` for `int`. The symmetric approach feels more natural and easier to understand.\n\nIt might also be worth adding a separate optimization for `HAnd` that checks whether the value is already within a certain range, like `[0, 31]` or narrower. There’s an existing [optimization](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:art/compiler/optimizing/instruction_simplifier.cc;drc\u003d9c843a66d11d85e1f69e944f1b37314d3e47aab1;bpv\u003d1;l\u003d3515) that simplifies patterns like `And(And(v, const), 0x1f)` into `And(v, min(const, 0x1f))`.\n\nGiven that, it seems like my optimization could still be beneficial even for int cases. What do you think—does that make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "7ccbbf0f_16e8ea2c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5496,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 5496,
        "endChar": 57
      },
